# Status (2026-10-05): open; a design question (how a default names an earlier field).
# A field default is "like a parameter default" (spec 10.1), and a parameter default may read the
# earlier parameters (spec 6: `def f(a, b = 1, c = b + 1)`). A field default cannot read an earlier field:
#   error: wrong number of arguments for Parser.src (given 0, expected 1)   (json.sake: `undefined local variable or function `src``)
# Expected: either `len` is 3 (as `def initialize(src, len = src.bytesize)` in Ruby), or the spec says
# a field default sees no fields.
class Parser
  attr_reader src, len
  def initialize(p) = @len = String.bytesize(src)
end
p Parser.len(Parser.new("abc"))
